WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:03.324
It was late at night.

2
00:00:03.325 --> 00:00:10.147
Dr. Dean McGreen was working in his lab in his barn.

3
00:00:10.148 --> 00:00:15.244
"This will change the world, Walden," Dr. McGreen said to his dog.

4
00:00:15.245 --> 00:00:18.907
"Most cars burn fuel, which causes pollution.

5
00:00:18.908 --> 00:00:22.515
But my new fuel will change everything.

6
00:00:22.516 --> 00:00:25.713
Cars won't make pollution anymore!"

7
00:00:25.714 --> 00:00:27.891
Dr. McGreen set down a beaker.

8
00:00:27.892 --> 00:00:30.389
He lit a flame to heat up the chemicals in it.

9
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.249
The chemicals bubbled.

10
00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:35.258
Walden barked.

11
00:00:35.259 --> 00:00:40.758
"Hush, Walden." Dr. McGreen picked up a flask that held another chemical.

12
00:00:40.759 --> 00:00:44.837
"I need to add exactly three drops to this flask."

13
00:00:44.838 --> 00:00:48.764
Dr. McGreen used an eyedropper to collect some of the bubbling chemicals. "Any

14
00:00:48.765 --> 00:00:53.874
more than three drops and the barn could explode!" Vroom,

15
00:00:53.875 --> 00:00:58.675
vroom! Outside, someone was riding a motorcycle. Dr.

16
00:00:58.676 --> 00:01:01.953
McGreen squeezed one drop into the flask. Then

17
00:01:01.954 --> 00:01:04.650
he squeezed another. Vroom,

18
00:01:04.651 --> 00:01:11.787
vroom! The motorcycle's engine was so loud, the barn walls shook. "Just

19
00:01:11.788 --> 00:01:16.329
one more drop!" Walden

20
00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:21.062
barked as Dr. McGreen squeezed the eyedropper. Poof!

21
00:01:21.063 --> 00:01:23.980
There was a bright flash. Then

22
00:01:23.981 --> 00:01:29.177
the flask exploded! ***

23
00:01:29.178 --> 00:01:31.935
"Where's Terrell?" Mara said.

24
00:01:31.936 --> 00:01:36.750
Roxy shrugged. "I'm not sure. He's pretty late, though."

25
00:01:36.751 --> 00:01:39.858
Roxy was in her backyard with Jack and Mara.

26
00:01:39.859 --> 00:01:43.921
Nearby was a cardboard box, aluminum foil, and scissors.

27
00:01:43.922 --> 00:01:47.573
The friends were making a solar oven for a school project.

28
00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:51.608
"I'm here!" Terrell hurried into the backyard.

29
00:01:51.609 --> 00:01:56.166
"And I brought the tape. Sorry I'm late. I had to walk.

30
00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:58.868
My mom's car wouldn't start."

31
00:01:58.869 --> 00:02:00.995
"That’s okay," Roxy said.

32
00:02:00.996 --> 00:02:04.036
"The wait will make our pizza taste better!"

33
00:02:04.037 --> 00:02:06.454
Jack frowned at the cardboard box.

34
00:02:06.455 --> 00:02:10.366
"Can we really cook a pizza by leaving it in that box?"

35
00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:16.456
"Yes," Terrell said. "The foil will reflect the sunlight and heat up the pizza.

36
00:02:16.457 --> 00:02:20.933
Cooking them this way will take longer than using a regular oven.

37
00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:24.142
But solar cooking is better for the environment."

38
00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:30.286
"Solar energy is clean energy," Roxy said. "No pollution!"

39
00:02:30.287 --> 00:02:34.376
Jack rubbed his belly. "When can we eat?" Mara

40
00:02:34.377 --> 00:02:39.818
laughed. "We need to build the solar oven first! Let's

41
00:02:39.819 --> 00:02:42.921
measure the sides of the box." Roxy’s

42
00:02:42.922 --> 00:02:50.973
watch beeped. "I, uh, think I left the measuring tape inside." Roxy

43
00:02:50.974 --> 00:02:54.892
ran inside and flipped open her watch. Mayor

44
00:02:54.893 --> 00:02:58.236
Bloom appeared. He was at home. "Mayor

45
00:02:58.237 --> 00:03:02.493
Bloom, what's the emergency?" Roxy asked. "My

46
00:03:02.494 --> 00:03:07.242
car won't start," Mayor Bloom said. "That

47
00:03:07.243 --> 00:03:11.908
doesn't sound like an emergency, Mayor," Roxy said. "

48
00:03:11.909 --> 00:03:16.231
All the cars in Metro City won’t start!" Mayor Bloom said.

49
00:03:16.232 --> 00:03:20.621
"Rocket Girl, I need you to find out what’s wrong."

50
00:03:20.622 --> 00:03:27.656
"No problem, Mayor. I’ll figure out what's going on!"

